# The receiver in swap() is an object of the family or a text. For the text the built-in is handed a callback that nobody knows, so the site may enter unseen code; the objects of the family do not leave with it and
# their methods have not escaped. While such a site forgot its shared calls, the method of A had one call that anybody listed, the direct one: it counted as called from one place, as run at most once, and its body
# took what that caller leaves, though swap() enters it too.
